    "text": "A proton of mass $m$ moving with a speed $v$ ( $< < $ c. velocity of light in vacuum) completes circular orbit in time $T$ in a uniform Whetic ficld. If the speed of the proton is increased to $\\sqrt{2}$ v, what will be time needed to plete the circular orbit?",
